            <ArticleTitle>High-density lipoprotein cholesterol and vascular stiffness at baseline in the activity counseling trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>104-7, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a middle-aged patient population, age was associated with stiffer vessels and high-density lipoprotein cholesterol with more elastic vessels. High-density lipoprotein cholesterol may be an indirect indicator of aerobic capacity or of less atherosclerosis, suggesting mechanisms for preserving vascular integrity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
